  "security_implications": "The adapter gates register read/write strobes (re_o, we_o) with err_internal, which is intended to block access on integrity or instruction errors. If err_internal is not correctly asserted (U1), unauthorized register access may occur. Additionally, addr_o is forced to word alignment with no generation of addr_align_err (U2). This could allow an out-of-alignment TileLink request to silently target a different word, bypassing any upstream address-range or access-control checks, potentially leading to data corruption or privilege escalation. The integrity protection parameters (CmdIntgCheck, EnableRspIntgGen, EnableDataIntgGen) indicate that the adapter's error-handling path is security-critical, but the logic driving err_internal is absent from this region.",
